From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tutor Trellis <noreply@tutortrellis.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 14:19:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] feat(mobile/system-pip): keep the camera on in the
 background while the window shows

As video call apps do: when the app goes to the background and iOS's picture
in picture window will show the call, our camera stays on, provided iOS lets
it run meanwhile (multitasking camera access on its capture session: iOS 18+
apps with the voip background mode, iPads with Stage Manager on an external
display, or Apple's entitlement; react-native-webrtc asks for it with its
enableMultitaskingCameraAccess option). The native module's
cameraMultitasking(streamURL) asks the camera's own capture session each time
the camera starts.

Otherwise the camera goes off as the app leaves, as before, now also while
sharing the screen (base/media kept it on then, but iOS stops it, so the
others saw a frozen picture). If the window doesn't open, or closes while the
app is still away, the camera goes off then. Coming back turns it on again.
